<title>USA: Sequana, Glaxo sign collaboration.</title>
<headline>Sequana, Glaxo sign collaboration.</headline>
<dateline>LA JOLLA, Calif. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequana Therapeutics Inc on Tuesday said its unit, NemaPharm Inc, and Glaxo Wellcome Plc have agreed to collaborate on gene functional analysis using NemaPharm's nematode worm C. elegans.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome is obligated to provide payments for full research support, as well as milestones based on NemaPharm targets that become part of drug discovery programs at Glaxo.</p>
<p>Royalties will be paid if products are developed from targets identified through the use of NemaPharm technology.</p>
</text>
